issues with sequencer's current todo script creation
  * revision handling (multiple branches, --ancestry-path, --first-parent, etc.)
  * assumes a checkout will happen ("reset onto"), which is broken; I shouldn't
    need to check out my new base before starting
  * uses the name "onto" even if it'll be used for a cherry-pick operation
  * uses "merge" directive for merge commits, which is like using "commit"
    directive instead of "pick"/"play"
  * "play"
    * "play" should be allowed to have multiple recorded $COMMIT arguments,
      (and the todo_item shouldn't just have a offset_in_buf to allow me to
       re-parse hex strings into commits which is wasted work)
    * "play" and "reset" are the only commands that should take a $COMMIT
  * $COMMIT directives
    * "edit" should be synonym for "break", i.e. it should be preceded by a "pick" directive.
    * "reword" should come by itself on the line after
    * "fixup" should also come by itself on line after
    * "squash" also should avoid a commit directive, but then it just becomes an abbreviation
      for a combination of a "fixup" directive on one line followed by a "reword" directive.
    * _only_ play & reset should take commits
   * requirement to iterate over all commits before even starting to
     replay, rather than replaying as we go (only cases we need to
     iterate all (remaining) commits is when generating the script for
     interactive display or for saving state)
  * First instruction should _always_ be "reset", second is "label" (unless
    replaying onto root?).  When pausing for conflicts or breaking/editing,
    need to reinsert a new "reset"/"label" instruction.  (We may even consider
    erroring out if first instruction is not a reset.  Done by setting onto to
    NULL.)

  * separation of todo_list_rearrange_squash() means re-parsing commits, which
    is wasted effort.  Should be done as part of making the original script.

ideas:
  * --interactive should be the default
  * accept `--todo $FILE` to let users directly pass todo list
  * --keep-base (don't readjust base of any commits; removes need for --onto)
  * --replay-base OLDBASE (don't readjust parents of any commits, unless that
    parent is OLDBASE)
  * only count things taking a commit (play/squash/fixup/reword) when reporting
    progress
  * allow users to "update-ref <refname>" without "from <hash>"

cool command lines (seen contains topics which contain ab/submodule-cleanup):
  * git replay --contained --keep-base --ancestry-path ab/submodule-cleanup..seen
      OR
    git replay --keep-base --first-parent ^next seen topic_branch



