Changes:
  * conflicts:
    * must read in index in order to write working tree/index
    * use sparse-as-possible worktree

  * todo list
    * no "merge" directive, at first
    * use "play" instead of "pick"
    * play <merge-hash> relative to <label or secondary hash>

    * implementation:
      * make parse_insn_line() non-static
      * add "play" directive, which accepts extra arguments for merges
      * use parse_insn_line() and todo_list_parse_insn_buffer()



  * git replay ${MERGE}^!: must assume remerging the same 2nd parent
  
  * state gets store in .git/replay-${worktree} (or .git/replay for main wrktr)
  * XDL_MERGE_PREFER_BASE if using diff3 conflict markers?
  * xdiff modifications:
    * conflict markers for remerge of old merge should exactly match conflict
      markers for new merge (by using the newer commit ids).  No extra indent
      either.
    * if there are no conflict marker blocks in any of the three sides for
      the region under consideration, do normal three-way merge stuff
    * when xdiff attempts to split up regions where the files differ, do not
      allow getting a subset of conflict marker blocks -- must grab that whole
      region
    * if conflict marker blocks of new merge exactly match auto-remerge, then
      we can take resolution from merge being replayed...
    * otherwise, take the conflict marker block from new merge, and ignore both
      the auto-remerge and the text from the merge being replayed.
      (ensures we don't get deeper nestings of conflicts)
    * if we take the otherwise above, point users at
      "git show --remerge-diff $ORIG_MERGE" for tips on resolving conflicts